jurisdiction":{"id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#US","kind":"const_ref"},"kind":"source_work","labels":[{"language":"en","status":"official","text":"5 U.S.C. §6103 — Holidays"}],"number":"5 U.S.C. 6103","package":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays","sourceKind":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#law"},{"contentHash":"sha256:93bd42a1a8e97bd1904df460a5c67f5b7297bd76045f22effb151139d2bfe660","id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_2023","kind":"source_edition","labels":[{"language":"en","status":"official","text":"United States Code, 2023 Edition"}],"language":"en","lifecycle":[{"extent":"1966-09-06","status":"adopted"}],"materializationStatus":"PINNED_UNOFFICIAL_COPY","officiality":"official","package":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays","work":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103"},{"contentHash":"sha256:23fbc23fca820d71be2e7a0d7273a2a3975402535ad187220b15ee4514539777","edition":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_2023","fragmentKind":"article","id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_A","kind":"fragment","locator":"article/6103/subsection/a","package":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays","texts":[{"contentHash":"sha256:3be104308a9fafc13e54ce9fad571a8ad9788d6201927af4112bdd8cd767ef92","language":"en","status":"official","text":"(a) The following are legal public holidays:\nNew Year's Day, January 1.\nBirthday of Martin Luther King, Jr., the third Monday in January.\nWashington's Birthday, the third Monday in February.\nMemorial Day, the last Monday in May.\nJuneteenth National Independence Day, June 19.\nIndependence Day, July 4.\nLabor Day, the first Monday in September.\nColumbus Day, the second Monday in October.\nVeterans Day, November 11.\nThanksgiving Day, the fourth Thursday in November.\nChristmas Day, December 25."}]},{"contentHash":"sha256:09c88a6e6c7cac0cf7be65e5b40f45918240a61077fb85c264334ac339c1ae28","edition":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_2023","fragmentKind":"article","id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_B1","kind":"fragment","locator":"article/6103/subsection/b/paragraph/1","package":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays","texts":[{"contentHash":"sha256:030b9ea4609a97d66bb24132cdb3f052bf250973a5ae998bffc3fb6c50ce604c","language":"en","status":"official","text":"(b) For the purpose of statutes relating to pay and leave of employees, with respect to a legal public holiday and any other day declared to be a holiday by Federal statute or Executive order, the following rules apply:\n(1) Instead of a holiday that occurs on a Saturday, the Friday immediately before is a legal public holiday for—\n(A) employees whose basic workweek is Monday through Friday; and\n(B) the purpose of section 6309 1 of this title."}]},{"contentHash":"sha256:c7532934d1c540cab7c291793fe1b070dc5f38385e7459bd7ff470fb97b2ff06","documentHash":"sha256:bad3ead1c6fb9c6df242142faa6af1cf919f90372780e1c4d7b24cedbdd03a43","edition":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_2023","id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#USC_5_6103_TEXT","kind":"publication","mediaType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","package":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays","retrievedAt":"2026-08-28T09:00:00Z","uri":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title5/html/USCODE-2023-title5-partIII-subpartE-chap61-subchapI-sec6103.htm"},{"contentHash":"sha256:bf553c14823b5dae7d1b7bc2a027cc386390deb6f237c8160dc21fdddc67696d","id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#VeteransDay","kind":"symbol_decl","labels":[{"language":"en","status":"unofficial","text":"Veterans Day"}],"name":"VeteransDay","package":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays","parameters":[],"returnType":{"name":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#Holiday"},"symbolKind":"constant","value":{"id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#VeteransDay","kind":"entity_ref"}},{"contentHash":"sha256:6e129371dad4a0387c420948c5549fc4e5005c44bb665451cfed6cc0c45c64b2","id":"urn:us:code:clir:federal-holidays#WashingtonsBirthday","kind":"symbol_decl","labels":[{"language